# The Epistemic Humility Theory of Everything (Corrected)

---

## IN PLAIN LANGUAGE

### The Core Idea

**We don't discover nature. We name it. And the only reason our naming matters is that we need each other to survive.**

Everything we think we "discover" is actually something we first learned to name, then forgot we named it, and then called it a discovery. But beneath all our naming sits one undeniable fact: **we are social creatures who must live together.** That fact—not logic, not reason, not science—is the real foundation of everything we think and do.

---

## THE REVISED HIERARCHY

| **Level** | **What It Is** | **Why It Matters** |
|:---|:---|:---|
| 1. The Elements | Raw existence | The given—we don't know what it is, only that it is |
| 2. Survival | Staying alive | The most basic drive of all living things |
| 3. Social Survival | Living together | Humans cannot survive alone; we are interdependence |
| 4. **Ethics** | **How we treat each other** | **The FOUNDATION—everything else serves this** |
| 5. Consciousness | Awareness of self and others | Emerges from social life |
